WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.001
-Our first guests tonight

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.837
are "New York Times"
best-selling authors

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.438
and the hosts of "Desus &amp; Mero,"

00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.106
which airs Thursday nights
on Showtime.

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:08.408
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:11.177
our friends Desus Nice
and The Kid Mero.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.678
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:22.688 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:29.896 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:34.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.337
-Gentlemen, this is my favorite
kind of week

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.338
because I have already
seen you this week.

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:40.807
-That's right.
We're revisiting.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.775
-We're revisiting.
Yesterday, we filmed something

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:46.379
for your show, and you took me
to a New York institution.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:48.447
-One of the
top cultural landmarks

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.216
in all of New York City.
-And based on the name,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.584
I think people
who don't live in New York

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.187
would be surprised this is
a New York City institution.

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.356
-Right. It sounds like
a regional place, but it's not.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.856
It's international
and in our hearts.

00:00:57.856 --> 00:01:00.493
-Where did you take me?
-We took him to Dallas BBQ.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:01.660
-That's right, baby.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.229
Dallas BBQ.
Know what I'm saying?

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.198
-And if you're not familiar
with Dallas BBQ,

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:08.167
it's where you can get
a 64-ounce margarita.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:09.501
-Yeah.
-Why would you want

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:12.505
a 64-ounce margarita on
a Tuesday morning at 11:00 a.m.?

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.674
-Well, that's what we drank.
Everything --

00:01:15.674 --> 00:01:17.109
It's Texas-style,
is how they describe it.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.511
-Texas-style.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.313
-They -- you could not lift
these with one hand.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.081
-No, no, no, no, no.
-It's like holding a newborn.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.550
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.586
-You really work out your arms.
-Really did.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.754
-There's so much sugar
in the drink --

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.255
that's why they do it --
so you can curl the drink

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:32.392
and burn calories.
-And often they come with

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.594
test tubes with an additional
shot of alcohol.

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:37.663
-That's right. But to keep it
classy, the small umbrella.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.132
-There was a very --
yeah, there was --

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:41.100
we had a lot of umbrellas
littering our table

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.002
at the end of the day.
And I will say,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.336
and I talked to both of you
backstage,

00:01:44.336 --> 00:01:46.572
I feel like my hangover
was way more from the sugar

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:47.706
in the BBQ drinks.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:49.508
-Absolutely.
-Oh, yeah, absolutely.

00:01:49.508 --> 00:01:51.878
My pancreas is gone.
It's gone.

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:54.447
-That was your favorite
of the organs!

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:56.615
-I always bragged about it.
-Yeah, I'm so sorry.

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.218
-I like my appendix.
-But you know what?

00:01:58.218 --> 00:01:59.985
You are a great person
to go drinking with.

00:01:59.985 --> 00:02:01.320
-Thank you.
-You can handle your liquor.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.388
You're not a lightweight.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.522
-Nope.
-Give it up for our guy Seth.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:04.557
-Thank you very much.
[ Applause ]

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.858
I don't know if that's great.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:06.992
-I don't know
if that's great, either.

00:02:06.992 --> 00:02:09.328
-I don't know.
-It's like, "Eh, you drank

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:10.662
a gallon of
Long Island iced tea."

00:02:10.662 --> 00:02:12.264
-It's cool when you get old
and you can still drink

00:02:12.264 --> 00:02:14.334
like a 19-year-old, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.903
Last time you were here,
we were talking about Eric Adams

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.537
and the potential
that he would be our mayor.

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.440
He's our mayor. How do you guys
think he's doing?

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.242
-Uh, it feels like we elected
a club promoter.

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.445
[ Laughter ]
-It does.

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.281
-He's my favorite mayor so far
that has their ear pierced.

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.716
There's nothing wrong with that.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.751
We got that going for us.
-He's also one of the only

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:34.754
mayors I feel like could bust
into a big D.J. session

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.056
in a nightclub.
So I'm looking forward to that.

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:41.060
-You guys have both said
that he basically governs

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.195
like someone who only has
24 hours in New York City.

00:02:43.195 --> 00:02:44.730
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:48.100
It's crazy how many places he is
over the course of one day.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.936
-He just goes everywhere.
It's like he gets invites

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:52.305
in the e-mail that you would
usually be like,

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.639
"Eh, I don't want to do that."

00:02:53.639 --> 00:02:55.341
He's just like, "Yes, yes, yes,
yes, yes, yes, yes."

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.277
-He's liking the invites
in his spam box.

00:02:57.277 --> 00:02:58.444
-Yeah.
-He might show up

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.813
at your kid's bar mitzvah.
You don't know.

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:02.347
-He was at my kid's
sixth birthday party.

00:03:02.347 --> 00:03:03.516
I don't know how
he got the invite.

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.683
-And then he wanted five
minutes, right?

00:03:04.683 --> 00:03:06.219
He wanted to make a speech
about the vision.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:07.820
-And then he left with
the bottle he came with.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.622
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.524
-Of Similac.
Why'd he take the Similac?

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.726
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.296
-Obviously, a lot of people,

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:17.863
both who live
in New York City and don't,

00:03:17.863 --> 00:03:19.566
know that we have a problem
with our subway system.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.968
But there was a recent
improvement made.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.970
There was $30 million
spent on a stairway.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.372
-Yeah.
-Yes.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.674
-Were you guys excited about
this new beautiful stairway?

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:30.910
-Super excited.
-It's what we needed.

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.811
-It's just another
very long stairway

00:03:32.811 --> 00:03:34.413
for you to get masturbated on
by a homeless person.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:37.283
[ Laughter ]
Know what I'm saying?

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.718
-I mean,
some of us wanted new trains.

00:03:38.718 --> 00:03:40.219
Some of us, you know,
wanted safety.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.320
But they was like,
"No. Staircase."

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.654
-Staircase.
-"Enjoy."

00:03:42.654 --> 00:03:45.325
-"Hey, man! You know that song
'Stairway to Heaven'?

00:03:45.325 --> 00:03:48.494
Stairway to the Q train, bro."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.796
-Do you guys feel like
there's any solutions

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:53.265
to our subway problems
here in New York City?

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.501
-Like, I don't know.
Like, spend some of the money

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.403
that you guys
have in your coffers?

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:59.171
-Probably depends
what we think the problem is.

00:03:59.171 --> 00:04:01.274
Is it trains running late?
Or perhaps --

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:02.542
'cause the other night,
I was drunk on a train,

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.976
and I was like,
"There's a lot of rats."

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.479
So if we release cats
to eat the rats...

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:07.680
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.415
-Your solution is more cats?

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:11.017
-You'll hear more about it
when I run for mayor.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.651
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:15.321
-Let's not give it away yet.
Let's not give it away.

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:18.524
[ Applause ]

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.793
Just like, all of a sudden,
just that beautiful stairway

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.061
and just thousands of cats
descending.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:26.966
-Meow!
-A lot of track fires.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.603
-I talked to you guys about this
yesterday when I saw you.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:32.238
You had a fantastic interview

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:34.073
with Denzel Washington
on your show.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.609
And what was wonderful about it,
it was a side of him

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.110
that I feel like
we don't see that often.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.411
He's obviously
a very serious man.

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:42.180
He's one of our greatest
living actors.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.051
But he mostly just talked about
different train stations

00:04:45.051 --> 00:04:46.619
in the Bronx with you guys.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.020
-That was not Denzel Washington
the actor,

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.389
that was Denzel the New Yorker.
-Yeah.

00:04:50.389 --> 00:04:53.993
-It's a whole different Denzel.
-"I'm D from Mount Vernon."

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:55.995
[ Laughter ]
-Did he warm into it,

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.496
or did he show up
like that immediately?

00:04:57.496 --> 00:05:00.299
-He just came in there, 'cause
he knew we're from the Bronx --

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:01.867
BX all day --
and he's from Mount Vernon,

00:05:01.867 --> 00:05:04.170
which is located
right above the Bronx.

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.872
So he already
felt that energy that, you know,

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:08.007
if you're not from New York,
it's the worst energy

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.308
you can ever see.

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:10.976
It's when two New Yorkers
link up together in a room.

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.279
-Oh, yeah.
-You're gonna hear a lot of loud

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:16.248
and a lot of, "Hey, we got pizza
in New York at 4:00 a.m.

00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:17.883
You don't have that down here."

00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:20.620
So, he just comes in,
and it was like hanging out

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:21.854
with your uncle.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.089
He was just, like,
so conversational and just warm.

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:25.991
-Very chill.
He walked in, he saw the bodega,

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:28.060
he's like,
"I recognize this environment.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.929
My guard is down."
-And then everything

00:05:29.929 --> 00:05:32.398
Denzel says, he says it
with a certain gravitas,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.667
so even if it's not serious,
you have to take it

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:37.236
really serious 'cause he's like,
"If you gonna get coffee,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:40.473
get it light -- or sweet."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.541
You're like, "What?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.541 --> 00:05:44.744
-All right.
-You just be on the train home,

00:05:44.744 --> 00:05:48.014
like, "Denzel,
got to get it together, bro.

00:05:48.014 --> 00:05:49.715
Can't be mixing these two."

00:05:49.715 --> 00:05:51.818
-"Can't have a fluffernutter
with no peanut butter."

00:05:51.818 --> 00:05:53.752
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:55.221
But he says it with the grav--
You know what I mean?

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.622
-Yeah.
-He says it in, like,

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.390
a "Training Day" voice.
You're like, "Oh!"

00:05:58.390 --> 00:05:59.692
-You're like,
"Okay, yeah, that's right.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.226
Yeah, no, it's peanut butter
and marshmallow stuff.

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:03.795
Yeah, you're right."
-You guys did not have Rihanna

00:06:03.795 --> 00:06:05.831
on the show, but you did have
a baby shower for her.

00:06:05.831 --> 00:06:07.333
-We did.
-That was very nice.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:08.935
-You know, 'cause we did that
thing where you throw people

00:06:08.935 --> 00:06:10.535
a baby shower
that they're not invited to.

00:06:10.535 --> 00:06:12.171
-Yeah.
-So she didn't show up.

00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:14.574
-Did Eric Adams show up?
-I think so!

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.476
-He's there.
He's still there.

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:18.076
They already broke down the set,
he's still there.

00:06:18.076 --> 00:06:19.912
-He was the one that pointed out
Rihanna didn't show up.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.013
'Cause he was handling
the guest list.

00:06:21.013 --> 00:06:22.881
-There you go.
-But you know Rihanna.

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:25.317
-Yeah, I've been --
you know, I had a wonderful --

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:26.485
I went day drinking with her,

00:06:26.485 --> 00:06:27.753
much like I did
with you two gentlemen.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:30.089
And it lives in my memory.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.424
-Do you go day drinking a lot
with people?

00:06:32.424 --> 00:06:34.494
-I do it more than I should,
yeah.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.295
-I could tell you
that you need to stop that,

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:37.730
but what you need to do
is invite us.

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.365
-Yeah, next time,
I'll invite you.

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.300
Now, you guys, obviously,
you have not booked Rihanna,

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.569
but are you hoping
to be the first talk show

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.471
that has the baby on?
-Oh, yeah.

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.339
-I mean, you know,
maybe in utero, you know?

00:06:47.339 --> 00:06:48.641
I mean, actually,
no, he's been born.

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.709
-It's too late. Yeah,
you missed that opportunity.

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:51.977
-We were trying
to get him in the warmer.

00:06:51.977 --> 00:06:53.378
-The baby's not SAG yet.

00:06:53.378 --> 00:06:55.347
We're waiting for all this
stuff, but it's gonna happen.

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:56.648
It's gonna happen.
-Gotcha.

00:06:56.648 --> 00:06:58.351
That's obviously something
to look forward to.

00:06:58.351 --> 00:07:01.987
You guys, you've talked,
as well, about wanting

00:07:01.987 --> 00:07:06.058
to go to England and maybe
interviewing some royalty.

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:07.393
The Queen.
You want to start at the top.

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:08.461
-Right at the top.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:09.695
Can't start with, like,
the babies.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:10.996
-No, no, no.
-Got to go right for the top.

00:07:10.996 --> 00:07:13.933
-No dukes or whatever.
Just like straight to the Queen.

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.134
-You're just gonna
go right into it.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.402
-Yeah, you see how
we do interviews.

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.836
We make people comfortable.
-Yeah, that's true.

00:07:17.836 --> 00:07:20.039
-Just imagine the Queen,
she takes the crown off.

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.974
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.175
-[ British accent ]
Blimey, blokes!

00:07:23.175 --> 00:07:25.778
-Aye, mate!
Ay! Oi! Oi!

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.447
-Oi! You know who's
my favorite drill rapper?

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:30.082
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:32.251
-Oi, you listen
to that new Skepta, mate?

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:35.121
-Her P.R. person's like,
"Queen, calm down."

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:36.489
-"We're gonna
have to heavily edit this."

00:07:36.489 --> 00:07:38.557
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:40.826
-That would be very --
I mean, you couldn't take

00:07:40.826 --> 00:07:42.495
the Queen to BBQs,
I don't think.

00:07:42.495 --> 00:07:43.830
-Oh, we would have to.
-We'd have to.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.130
You know what?
I think you're afraid

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.632
that she would drink
more than you.

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.100
-I'm afraid --
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.070
I think anyone that age,
if they had one sip of those,

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.771
they might drop dead.
-We're going to jail.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:54.172
That's going to be
an international incident.

00:07:54.172 --> 00:07:56.142
-I really have to speak
to the --

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:59.045
I've also never seen
that color of cocktail

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.379
that we had yesterday.
-Oh, no.

00:08:00.379 --> 00:08:02.514
-Like you said, none of those
colors appear in nature.

00:08:02.514 --> 00:08:03.615
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:08:03.615 --> 00:08:04.683
They are all man-made.

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:06.018
-Right, they all appear, like,

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:08.220
when there's
been a reactor leak.

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.623
-Yeah, yeah.
-A lot of those food dyes,

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:12.090
if you looked at
the bottle that they came in,

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:14.059
they were like
"Do not handle without gloves"?

00:08:14.059 --> 00:08:16.629
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:19.731
-This is the first time I've
seen Jay Z blue in real life.

00:08:19.731 --> 00:08:22.401
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:26.004
-Did you guys follow
the jubilee, the big --

00:08:26.004 --> 00:08:28.007
-[ Scoffs ]
Me and all the homies.

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:29.342
-Yeah, hell yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:31.577
-Jubilee, fam!
-A jubilee viewing party?

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.513
-At Dallas BBQs.
-Yeah.

00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:36.548
[ Laughter ]
We had our own jubilee.

00:08:36.548 --> 00:08:39.285
-Oh, I saw this, the Ju-BB --
the Ju-BB-Lee.

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:41.254
-The Ju-BBQ-Lee.

00:08:41.254 --> 00:08:44.356
-Yeah, the Ju-BBQ-Lee
viewing party.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:45.625
And you guys hosted it.
-We hosted it,

00:08:45.625 --> 00:08:47.559
and we dressed up
like Queen Elizabeth.

00:08:47.559 --> 00:08:49.128
[ Laughter ]
-Yes.

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:50.228
-And she didn't show up.

00:08:50.228 --> 00:08:51.497
-Now, do you guys
get in trouble?

00:08:51.497 --> 00:08:52.764
Can you get canceled for that,

00:08:52.764 --> 00:08:54.033
dressing up
like Queen Elizabeth?

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.834
I think, like, you might
be in the clear, right?

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:57.569
-I mean, it depends on what kind
of look you pull off.

00:08:57.569 --> 00:08:59.071
-Yeah.
-I feel like people would

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.406
just be like,
"Oh, they're Madea."

00:09:00.406 --> 00:09:01.607
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:09:01.607 --> 00:09:04.576
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, there's a chance.

00:09:04.576 --> 00:09:06.379
-I don't know if it would work.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:08.113
-You know, if you see me
in compression stockings,

00:09:08.113 --> 00:09:09.214
that might just be
'cause I'm old.

00:09:09.214 --> 00:09:10.782
-Yeah, all right.
Well, we're all getting

00:09:10.782 --> 00:09:12.017
a little bit older,
but it's still wonderful

00:09:12.017 --> 00:09:13.151
to have you guys around.

00:09:13.151 --> 00:09:14.353
Thank you so much
for spending time with us.

00:09:14.353 --> 00:09:15.654
-Thank you, Seth!
-I can't wait to see the show

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:16.822
this Thursday.

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.691
Desus Nice, The Kid Mero,
everybody!

00:09:18.691 --> 00:09:22.427
"Desus &amp; Mero" airs
Thursday nights on Showtime.

00:09:22.427 --> 00:09:24.496
It's never anything
but fantastic.

00:09:24.496 --> 00:09:26.365
We'll be right back
with Jensen Ackles.

